        "transliteration": "wa bikum akhrajana allahu min aldhdhulli wa farraja `anna ghamarati alkurubi wa anqadhana min shafa jurufi alhalakati wa min alnnari bi'abi antum wa ummi wa nafsi bimuwalatikum `allamana allahu ma`alima dinina wa aslaha ma kana fasada min dunyana wa bimuwalatikum tammat alkalimatu wa `azumat alnni`matu wa'talafat alfurqatu wa bimuwalatikum tuqbalu altta`atu almuftaradatu wa lakum almawaddatu alwajibatu walddarajatu alrrafi`atu walmaqamu almahmudu walmakanu alma`lumu `inda allahi `azza wa jalla waljahu al`azimu walshsha'nu alkabiru walshshafa`atu almaqbulatu rabbana amanna bima anzalta",
        "english": "It is on account of you that Allah has pulled us out of degradation, removed from us the clutches of hardships, and saved us from the brink of the pit of perditions and from the Fire. May my father, mother, and soul be ransoms for you. Through our loyalty to your leadership, Allah has taught us the features of our religion and has set aright the spoiled items of our worldly lives. Through our loyalty to your leadership, the Word has been perfected, the grace has become great, and the discord has turned into alliance. Through our loyalty to your leadership, the obligatory obedience (to Allah) is accepted. To you alone are the obligatory affection, the elevated ranks, the praiseworthy standing, the renowned station with Allah the Almighty and All-majestic, the topmost prestige, the supreme station, and the admitted intercession. O our Lord, we believe in that which You have sent down",
